---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PUBLISHER, SITE } from '../consts';
import { simplePageBreadcrumb } from '../lib/schema';

const description = `Terms and Conditions of use for ${SITE.name}.com. Governs your use of our Apple guides, technical tutorials, software reviews, intellectual property, and limitations of liability.`;
const url = `${SITE.url}/terms-and-conditions/`;
---
<Base title="Terms & Conditions"
      {description} canonical={url} schema={[
        {
          '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': `${url}#webpage`, url,
          name: 'Terms & Conditions', description,
          isPartOf: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#website` },
        },
        simplePageBreadcrumb('/terms-and-conditions/', 'Terms & Conditions'),
      ]}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Terms &amp; Conditions</nav>
    <div class="prose" style="padding:34px 0 10px">
      <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 2 October 2026. Effective date: 2 October 2026.</p>

      <h2>1. Introduction and Agreement to Terms</h2>
      <p>
        Welcome to <strong>{SITE.name}.com</strong> ("{SITE.name}", "the Site", "we", "us", or "our"), operated by <strong>{PUBLISHER.legalName}</strong>, a {PUBLISHER.companyType.toLowerCase()} registered in {PUBLISHER.jurisdiction} under company registration number {PUBLISHER.companyNumber}, with its registered office at {PUBLISHER.address.street}, {PUBLISHER.address.city}, {PUBLISHER.address.postcode}, {PUBLISHER.address.country}.
      </p>
      <p>
        These Terms and Conditions govern your access to and use of {SITE.name}.com, including all content, tutorials, technical guides, reviews, and associated services. By accessing or browsing this website, you confirm that you accept these Terms and agree to comply with them. If you do not agree to these Terms, you must not use our website.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Nature of Content &amp; Technical Tutorial Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name}.com is an independent digital publication providing educational tutorials, hardware analysis, troubleshooting steps, and software reviews focused on iOS, iPadOS, macOS, watchOS, and related Apple technologies.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Educational Purpose Only:</strong> All content, including step-by-step guides, terminal scripts, system settings adjustments, and battery preservation advice, is published strictly for informational and educational purposes. While our editorial team rigorously tests configurations on genuine hardware, we make no representations or warranties of any kind—express or implied—regarding the accuracy, completeness, or suitability of the information for your specific device configuration.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>User Responsibility and Backups:</strong> Apple operating systems undergo frequent point updates and beta cycle changes that may alter menu locations, feature availability, or system behaviors. Any configuration adjustments, terminal commands, or device management workflows you execute are undertaken at your sole discretion and risk. We strongly advise all readers to maintain complete, verified backups (via iCloud Backup or macOS Time Machine) prior to undertaking significant device reconfiguration.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Intellectual Property Rights</h2>
      <p>
        Unless otherwise indicated, {SITE.name}.com and its original editorial content, articles, custom illustrations, site design, and compilation are the exclusive property of {PUBLISHER.legalName} and are protected by United Kingdom, European, and international copyright, trademark, and intellectual property laws.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Permitted Personal Use:</strong> You are granted a limited, revocable, non-exclusive license to access and read our articles for your personal, non-commercial use. You may print individual pages for personal reference or share links to our content.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Prohibited Actions:</strong> You may not copy, reproduce, republish, distribute, broadcast, transmit, mirror, scrape, or create derivative works from our articles without express prior written consent from {PUBLISHER.legalName}. Automated data mining, web scraping, or feeding site content into artificial intelligence training datasets without an express commercial license is strictly prohibited.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Trademark Disclaimer:</strong> Apple, iPhone, iPad, Mac, macOS, Apple Watch, watchOS, iPadOS, AirPods, AirTag, ProRAW, ProRes, and Face ID are registered trademarks of Apple Inc., registered in the United States and other countries. {SITE.name}.com is an independent publication and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Apple Inc. All other third-party trademarks, logos, and app names cited belong to their respective owners and are referenced under nominative fair use for descriptive and editorial critique purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Acceptable Use Policy</h2>
      <p>When using {SITE.name}.com, you agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the site in any way that violates any applicable local, national, or international law or regulation.</li>
        <li>Engage in any automated data gathering, scraping, harvesting, or crawling of site infrastructure without prior written authorization.</li>
        <li>Attempt to interfere with the proper functioning, security, or network connectivity of the site, including through denial-of-service (DoS) attacks or introducing malware or malicious code.</li>
        <li>Impersonate any person or entity, or misrepresent your affiliation with any person or organization.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Advertising and Affiliate Relationships</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name}.com is supported by digital display advertising (including Google AdSense) and contextual affiliate partnerships.
      </p>
      <p>
        When an article includes affiliate links, a clear disclosure notice is displayed. If you make a purchase through these links, we may receive a commission from the merchant or platform at no additional cost to you.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our commercial arrangements do not influence our editorial assessments, hardware ratings, or critical recommendations. For details on our editorial standards, please review our <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>. For information on how advertising partners use cookies, please see our <a href="/cookies-privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Links to External Third-Party Websites</h2>
      <p>
        Our articles contain hyperlinks to third-party websites, including developer portals, the Apple App Store, and external resources. These links are provided solely for your convenience and context. {SITE.name}.com exercises no control over the content, uptime, security, or terms of third-party websites, and we assume no liability for any loss or damage arising from your use of them.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, in no event shall {PUBLISHER.legalName}, its directors, editors, writers, employees, or agents be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, including without limitation:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Loss of data, files, or digital backups;</li>
        <li>Device malfunction, unexpected software restarts, or performance degradation;</li>
        <li>Loss of profits, revenue, or business opportunities;</li>
        <li>Any interruption or cessation of transmission to or from our website.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Nothing in these Terms shall exclude or limit our liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, fraudulent misrepresentation, or any other liability that cannot be excluded or limited under English law.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to defend, indemnify, and hold harmless {PUBLISHER.legalName} and its editorial contributors from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, judgments, awards, losses, costs, expenses, or fees (including reasonable legal fees) arising out of or relating to your violation of these Terms or your use of the website.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Governing Law and Jurisdiction</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms and Conditions, their subject matter, and their formation are governed by the laws of England and Wales. You and {PUBLISHER.legalName} agree that the courts of England and Wales shall have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any dispute or claim arising out of or in connection with these Terms, except that consumers resident in other jurisdictions retain the benefit of mandatory consumer protection provisions of their local law.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Modifications to Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to revise and amend these Terms at our discretion. The most current version will always be maintained at <a href={url}>{url}</a>, with the effective revision date indicated at the top. Your continued use of the website following the posting of revised Terms constitutes your acceptance of the changes.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact Information</h2>
      <p>
        If you have any questions, feedback, or legal inquiries concerning these Terms and Conditions, please contact us:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.contactEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.contactEmail}</a> or <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.editorialEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.editorialEmail}</a></li>
        <li><strong>Postal Address:</strong> {PUBLISHER.legalName}, {PUBLISHER.address.street}, {PUBLISHER.address.city}, {PUBLISHER.address.postcode}, {PUBLISHER.address.country}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
